Rope AV5 contains, unmodified, the Lean sources of "A classification of finite Euclidean
Ramsey configurations" (result 172 of the OpenAI math release):

  https://github.com/openai/math, commit fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb
  lean/OAI/Combinatorics/EuclideanRamsey/*.lean  ->  OAI/Combinatorics/EuclideanRamsey/*.lean
  lean/ComparatorChallenges/EuclideanRamsey.lean  ->  vendor/OAI-ComparatorChallenge-EuclideanRamsey.lean
                                                     and AV5Challenge/OAIClassification.lean
  lean/ComparatorChallenges/EuclideanRamseySpherical.lean
                                                  ->  vendor/OAI-ComparatorChallenge-EuclideanRamseySpherical.lean
                                                     and AV5Challenge/OAISpherical.lean
  LICENSE                                         ->  vendor/OAI-LICENSE

These files are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (vendor/OAI-LICENSE). They are
byte-identical to the upstream blobs at that commit (MANIFEST; `AV5_UPSTREAM=1 bash REPRODUCE`
re-checks this against GitHub). AV5Challenge/Main.lean and AV5Challenge/Equiv.lean repeat the
upstream challenge's definitions of Space, Congruent and Ramsey verbatim, and the
controls repeat them (one control redefines a constant on purpose). Apart from the file below, the
rope imports OpenAI's files and uses their lemmas as they are.

Modified file: Rope/SixPointCircle.lean (the circle helpers of the six-point case) adapts
lemmas of OpenAI's lean/OAI/Combinatorics/EuclideanRamsey/CircleGeometry.lean and
CircleExtension.lean (Apache License 2.0, Copyright OpenAI): ramsey_restrict, zero_radius_ramsey,
circle_coordinates, stereographic, stereographic_recover, stereographic_injective,
stereographic_on_circle and circle_infinite are copied into the namespace
OAI.EuclideanRamsey.SixPoint, and extend_to_five is generalized to extend_to_six (the target size 5
replaced by 6). The file's header and each lemma's docstring say so. That file is under the Apache
License, Version 2.0.

Everything else in this directory was written for this project and is under the MIT License
(the repository's LICENSE; see also the repository's NOTICE).
